      "description": "Watch Hannover 96 vs VfL Wolfsburg highlights and goals from 2. Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 16, 2026. Late Penalty Secures Dramatic Victory for Wolfsburg at Hannover The VfL Wolfsburg secured a hard-fought away victory against Hannover 96 in a tense encounter, with a crucial late penalty proving decisive. Tightly Contested First Half The match, played on August 16, 2026, began with both teams looking to establish control. The first half was characterized by solid defensive displays and a scarcity of clear-cut chances. The teams headed into the break with the scoreline unchanged, setting the stage for a more dynamic second half. Second Half Intensity and Yellow Cards The second period saw a noticeable increase in the game's intensity. Both sides made strategic substitutions in an attempt to break the deadlock. Hannover 96 and VfL Wolfsburg traded blows, but a combination of a lack of finishing touch and resolute defending kept the score at bay for much of the second half. Yellow cards were issued to Jean Hugonet , Vini Souza , and Jonas Adjetey , reflecting the physical nature of the contest. Late Drama Decides the Tie As the match drew to a close, a pivotal moment emerged in the dying minutes. In the 87th minute, VfL Wolfsburg was awarded a penalty kick. Fabian Reese held his nerve under pressure, converting the spot-kick to put his side ahead. Despite late efforts from Hannover 96 to find an equalizer, Reese's goal was the only one of the game. The referee's final whistle, after added time, confirmed the narrow and crucial away win for VfL Wolfsburg ."
